"about": "Compare ICICI Lombard Motor Insurance Plans"
}
</script>


<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does Motor Insurance cover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A motor package policy provides coverage for own damage and third-party liabilities. Under a motor insurance policy, losses or damages to the insured vehicle, caused due to natural and manmade disasters are covered. Personal Accident Cover is included in case of injury or death of registered owner-driver in any vehicle-related mishap."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the period for which a motor policy is issued?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Commonly, a motor insurance policy in India is issued for a period of 12 months, i.e. 1 year. However, for two-wheeler owners, it is now possible to opt for long-term motor insurance. IRDAI has introduced long-term two-wheeler insurance for a policy term of up to 3 years."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I cancel my claim?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "After filing a motor insurance claim, in case you wish to cancel the claim, you can reach us through any of the following modes: \n\tContact your insurance representative directly \n\tCall us on our toll free 1800 2666 for assistance \n\tReach out to us on customersupport@icicilombard.com \n"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if I do not have a motor insurance policy?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You must get a motor insurance policy for your own benefit. It’s not just the repair costs that you’ll have to bear in case of any damages, you may also have to pay a fine if you are caught driving without a valid motor vehicle insurance by the police.\nIt is easy to buy motor insurance online if you have your vehicle registration number. You can buy ICICI Lombard motor insurance either from our website or IL Insure app through the following steps:\n\tEnter the vehicle registration number and your contact details \n\tReview instant quote received for your motor insurance policy based on your vehicle type\n\tPay the premium if you’re happy with quote\n\t View and download policy instantly online\nWhen you buy vehicle insurance online, remember to look for add-on features that suit your need.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is motor insurance premium calculated?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Motor insurance premium for a vehicle is calculated on the basis of multiple factors, including the Insured Declared Value (IDV) of the vehicle, make and model of the vehicle, seating capacity, cubic capacity etc. The premium amount also depends on a few other factors such as the type of policy chosen, deductibles, and add-on covers. Third-party premiums are decided by the IRDAI.\nWhile choosing the motor insurance policy from an insurer, compare various coverages and their premiums to make the right choice.\n"
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>



